# Revisions that `git blame` should look straight through.
#
# One unabbreviated 40-character SHA per line. Lines starting with `#` and blank
# lines are ignored. Only commits that changed formatting and NOTHING else may
# be listed here — a commit with any behaviour change in it must never be made
# invisible to blame.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the repository root automatically and shows an
# "Ignoring revisions in .git-blame-ignore-revs" banner in the blame view.
# Git does not: locally it has to be pointed at the file once, per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#     git config blame.markIgnoredLines true      # optional: marks moved lines '?'
#
# Without that config, `git blame` locally will still attribute those lines to
# the formatting commit while github.com does not — a difference that has cost
# people an afternoon before.

